<h1>Special Symbols and Abbreviations</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p class="whs4">A macro command has name very close or identical to the real KUBE command. The command may or may not include parameters. In both cases some rules for writing commands in scripts should be kept.</p>
<ul>
<li style="font-family:Arial; font-size:10pt;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">If a command has parameters they should be enclosed in brackets.</p>
</li>
<li style="font-family:Arial; font-size:10pt;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Parameters are separated by commas and the correct parameter format should be kept.</p>
</li>
<li style="font-family:Arial; font-size:10pt;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">The order of parameters in a single command can be changed, it doesn't affect the command execution.</p>
</li>
<li style="font-family:Arial; font-size:10pt;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Every parameter has name and value divided by the equal sign (<span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;">=</span>).</p>
</li>
<li style="font-family:Arial; font-size:10pt;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Values for some of the parameters-strings (like file names) should be enclosed in quotes.</p>
</li>
<li style="font-family:Arial; font-size:10pt;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">If a line begins with <span style="font-family:'Courier New' , monospace;">//</span> it is assumed to be a comment and is omitted by the interpreter.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="whs4">Here follows a list of all symbols and abbreviations used in the script language:</p>
